-- title:
--   §II p.5: orbit-completed monomial encodings
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a subgroup of the permutations of $d$ features, and let $A$ be a squarefree support, that is, a subset of the feature indices. Let $\mathcal O=\{\sigma A:\sigma\in K\}$ contain each distinct support once. Define
--   $$E_A(x)=\exp\!\left[-\frac i2\sum_{B\in\mathcal O}\left(\prod_{i\in B}x_i\right)\left(\prod_{i\in B}Z_i\right)\right].$$
--   For every $\sigma\in K$, $E_A(\sigma x)=U_\sigma E_A(x)U_\sigma^\dagger$, with $U_\sigma$ the wire permutation. If the subgroup is generated by a translation $t$ with $t^d=1$, $d>0$, and $A$ has two sites, then $|\mathcal O|\le d$. This counts orbit terms, without asserting a gate complexity.
-- source:
--   Exploiting symmetry in variational quantum machine learning, arXiv:2205.06217v1, PDF p. 5, §II p.5: orbit-completed monomial encodings

